# Ukraine — first week of the Russian full-scale invasion, Feb 24–Mar 3 2022
#
# A workable post-2015 alternative to the Vietnam case study, since this
# event is in GDELT's coverage and the surviving articles are still
# directly fetchable. Useful for testing whether the tool can surface
# Russian state framing vs Western mainstream vs Russian-independent
# coverage of the same opening days.
#
# Usage:
#   python -m news_lens \
#       --urls-file examples/ukraine_feb_2022.urls \
#       --ollama --model qwen3:8b --max-concurrency 1 \
#       --html ukraine_feb_2022.html
#
# Outlets to source (replace placeholders with verified URLs — Wayback
# snapshots are often safer than live URLs for fast-moving events):
#
# Russian state-affiliated:
#   - RT, Feb 24 2022 — "Russia launches military operation in Ukraine"
#   - Sputnik / TASS — official statements published Feb 24
#
# Russian independent (later forced offline; Wayback snapshots survive):
#   - Meduza, Feb 24-25 2022 — front-page reporting
#   - Novaya Gazeta, Feb 24 2022 — front-page reporting
#
# Western mainstream:
#   - The New York Times, Feb 24 2022 — lead story
#   - The Guardian, Feb 24 2022 — live blog wrap or main report
#   - BBC News, Feb 24 2022 — main report
#
# Other perspectives:
#   - Al Jazeera English, Feb 24 2022
#   - Xinhua / Global Times, Feb 24 2022 — Chinese state framing
#   - Le Monde, Feb 24 2022
#
# What the comparison should surface:
#   - Universal claims (e.g. that Russian forces entered Ukraine on Feb 24)
#   - Disputed framings (special military operation vs invasion / war)
#   - Omissions (which side's casualties are foregrounded vs buried)
#   - Single-origin claims (Ministry of Defence press conferences taken as
#     fact by some outlets, attributed by others)
#
# --- replace below this line with one URL per article ---

# https://web.archive.org/web/2022.../rt.com/...
# https://web.archive.org/web/2022.../tass.com/...
# https://web.archive.org/web/2022.../meduza.io/...
# https://web.archive.org/web/2022.../novayagazeta.eu/...
# https://www.nytimes.com/2022/02/24/...
# https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/feb/24/...
# https://www.bbc.com/news/world-europe-...
# https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2022/2/24/...
# https://www.globaltimes.cn/page/202202/...
# https://www.lemonde.fr/international/article/2022/02/24/...
